@node Region of interest, , ,Images
@section Region of interest
@cindex Region of interest
@tindex ROI
@findex GetROI
@findex Shrink
@findex GetROIRowStart

All images contain a "region of interest" (ROI), that is, a record of how much of the image is valid. Many operations such as convolution give a resulting image that is smaller than the original (eg. by half the convolution kernel's size), and subsequent processing should only look at data inside the ROI.

An image's ROI is stored as a class which provides various functions for growing, shrinking and changing the size of the ROI. eg:

@example
   my_image.GetROI().Shrink(2);
@end example

would shrink the ROI of @code{my_image} by 2. To process only the ROI of an image, one might do as follows:

@example
   const VW::ROI roi = my_rgb_image.GetROI();
   for (unsigned int y = roi.Top(); y < roi.Bottom(); y++) @{
      typename VW::ImageRGB<unsigned char>::PixelPtr p = my_rgb_image.GetROIRowStart(y);

      for (unsigned int x = roi.Left(); x < roi.Right(); x++,p++) @{

         // Process pixel p
	 ...

      @}
   @}
@end example
